precision mismatch: expected f32, got f64

`likelihood_ratio_p_value` is the one Nautilus.Stats export that stays f32:
it calls `Nautilus.Distributions.chi_squared_cdf`, which is f32-only, and a
generic caller cannot be more generic than its callee (nautilus#70). This pins
that residue. When Distributions becomes Float-generic, this test starts to
fail as an unexpected pass. Convert `likelihood_ratio_p_value` then, and
delete this file.
